course: dictionary
lesson: 6547
title: The feel of something new
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Newness is a noun. It names a state, the state of being new or fresh. The ending -ness turns the describing word new into a name for that quality. «The caravan was shining with newness, painted a canary-yellow picked out with green, and red wheels.» Shining with newness means it looked brand new and fresh.
explain: Newness can also be a feeling. When a place is strange and you know nothing about it, you feel its newness. A new school, a new season or a new car can all carry newness. Ask yourself: is this fresh and just made, or is it unfamiliar to me?
explain: Look for clues around the word. In the caravan sentence, the bright colours and the word shining show that it is fresh and clean, not old and worn. Those clues tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Newness is a noun. The ending -ness turns the describing word new into a name for the quality.
fact: Newness is uncountable, so you say «the newness», not «a newness» or «newnesses».
fact: «Newness» can mean the state of being new or fresh, as in «shining with newness».
fact: «Newness» can also mean the feeling that something is unfamiliar, like a strange new town.
fact: Look for clues such as bright colours or words like «shining» to tell whether a text means fresh or strange.
exercise: «The caravan was shining with newness.» What does newness mean here? | *The state of being new and fresh | The weight of a heavy load | The sound of a motor | The feeling of being very old
exercise: Ella moved to a new town and felt the newness of every street. What does newness mean here? | A kind of food | *The feeling that everything is unfamiliar | The state of being very tired | The feeling that everything is cold
exercise: Find and copy the word that means the state of being new. | smelled | fresh | paint | *newness
test: What does the -ness ending do in newness? | It makes the word mean old | It makes the word a verb | It makes the word plural | *It turns the describing word new into a noun
test: Which sentence uses newness correctly? | Newness the car smiled. | *The newness of the car made Dad smile. | The newness cars are fast. | I newness the car yesterday.
exam: Why does the writer use «shining with newness» in the caravan sentence? | It tells us the caravan is parked in a field | *It tells us the caravan looks fresh and brand new | It tells us the caravan is very heavy | It tells us the caravan is old and broken
